history_summary_node.summary_text:
# Conversation Summary

## 1. Previous Conversation

The user requested replication of a specific webpage (https://axtira.webflow.io/home-one) with accurate layout and design. The AI successfully created a full replica using Vite, vanilla HTML/CSS, and JavaScript, including all major sections. The dev server was launched and is running on http://localhost:5173.

Throughout the conversation, the user requested several design iterations:
- Converting all colors to OKLCH color space
- Replacing the original black color (#15151f) with OKLCH equivalent of #06559f (blue)
- Creating complementary darker blue for section backgrounds with gradient
- Replacing all gold colors with OKLCH equivalent of #16dbe1 (cyan)
- Replacing "Axtira" text logo with `/altius-lifts.svg` image at 50px height
- Replacing warm cream background with ice-blue tint at 93% lightness
- Replacing emoji icons with Font Awesome icons
- Creating cobalt blue variable for H2 headings on light sections
- Restructuring hero to use full-width background image with overlay
- Adding hero image at `/hero1.webp` with grayscale filter
- Creating darker overlay variable for hero
- Aligning hero content to the left
- Integrating content-grid layout system (Kevin Powell / Ryan Mulligan pattern)
- Integrating Alpine.js with scroll animations using x-intersect plugin
- Reducing border-radius on all rounded buttons from 50px to var(--radius) (12px)
- Adding grayscale filter to hero background image

The user then made significant content changes behind the scenes, converting the energy/oil & gas site to a lift company (Altius Lifts) with real content about lift installation, maintenance, modernization, and repairs.

The user then requested renaming class names in the HTML to be more relevant to the subject of each element and adjusting the CSS accordingly. The AI completed this task, renaming various sections.

Following this, the user requested several display fixes and design improvements including fixing sectors section cards, adjusting text widths, adding dark containers, changing grid layouts, updating icons, and redesigning the services section as a tabbed carousel.

The user then requested various refinements including changing CTAs to text links, adding FAQ section with accordions, styling improvements, adding section tags/badges, replacing arrow icons with Font Awesome, and moving sector card numbers to top-right corners.

The user then requested decorative elements to break up the page. Initially, blueprint-style connectors were attempted but rejected. The final solution was simple vertical white lines positioned at 80% across the page (alternating to 20% on even dividers), with responsive height scaling.

Additional improvements included:
- Adding gradient to navbar on scroll
- Redesigning footer with 4 columns (logo/brand, Quick Links, Opening Hours, Contact Us)
- Adding gradient underlines to footer headings
- Adding gradients to service tab backgrounds
- Implementing auto-rotation for service tabs (20s delay, then 10s intervals)
- Animating the lists in the services section with staggered entrance effects
- Fixing auto-rotation timer issues with proper cleanup

## 2. Current Work

The user acknowledged that the page was "vibe coded" and requested a full audit to identify unused or overbloated code before rolling the design out to other website pages. The user asked whether to continue with the current agent or start fresh. The AI recommended continuing due to full context knowledge.

The AI was instructed to:
1. Audit index.html and style.css for unused code, redundancy, and DRY opportunities
2. Double check findings to ensure nothing in use is removed
3. Take opportunities for DRY and the creation of utility classes and components

The AI completed a comprehensive audit and presented findings in 4 categories:
1. **Dead Code** - Safe to remove (no HTML reference): ~160 lines including unused CSS variables (--dark-2, --gray-400), entire commented-out sections (#stats, #about, #sustainability), unused selectors (.section-tag, .badge-icon, .btn-dark, .btn-white, .hero-stats, .stat-*, .anim-fade-in), and dead responsive rules
2. **Redundancies** - Can be simplified: body color hardcoding, duplicate font-family, duplicate list-style resets, duplicate .arrow styles
3. **DRY Opportunities** - Extract reusable patterns: Badge/tag component, section heading utility, easing variable, white alpha opacity variables, glass card component
4. **Keep** - Verified as used: Dynamic Alpine.js classes (.scrolled, .in-view, .is-animating, .is-open, .active, .sc-enter*)

The user approved with a single word: "proceed"

The AI began Phase 1 of the cleanup, starting with structural removals and additions. The first edit was successfully applied:
- Changed body color from hardcoded `oklch(45.08%...)` to `var(--dark)`
- Changed body background from hardcoded `oklch(100% 0 none)` to `var(--white)`
- Reorganized CSS variables with comments for better organization
- Removed unused variables: `--dark-2`, `--gray-400`
- Added white alpha scale variables: `--white-04` through `--white-80` (14 new variables)
- Added easing variable: `--ease-out-expo: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`

The user then asked "What happened?" indicating the AI may have stalled or the progress wasn't visible.

## 3. Key Technical Concepts

- **Vite**: Modern build tool used for development server with hot module replacement
- **Vanilla JavaScript**: Used for navbar scroll effects
- **Alpine.js 3.x**: Lightweight JavaScript framework for reactive interactivity
- **Alpine.js x-intersect plugin**: Intersection Observer wrapper for scroll-triggered animations
- **Alpine.js x-collapse plugin**: Smooth height animation for accordions
- **Alpine.js x-data, x-show, x-transition, x-init, x-effect, :class**: Directives for state management, transitions, and reactive classes
- **CSS Custom Properties**: Used for theming (colors, spacing, radii) and animation timing (`--stagger`, `--delay`, `--li`, `--li-total`)
- **OKLCH Color Space**: CSS Color Level 4 color space - provides perceptually uniform colors with better interpolation than RGB/HSL
- **CSS Grid**: Primary layout system for sections
- **Content-Grid Layout System**: Kevin Powell / Ryan Mulligan intrinsic layout pattern using CSS Grid with named grid lines for content/breakout/full-width control
- **Flexbox**: Used for navbar, hero stats, and smaller component layouts
- **CSS Animations**: `@keyframes` for hero on-load animations and service panel content animations, CSS transitions for scroll-triggered animations
- **Intersection Observer API**: Wrapped by Alpine.js x-intersect plugin
- **Fixed Positioning**: Used for topbar and navbar with scroll behavior
- **CSS Gradients**: Linear gradients used for section backgrounds, navbar, footer, and service tabs
- **Font Awesome 6.5.1**: Icon library loaded via CDN
- **Cubic Bezier Easing**: `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)` for smooth, natural animations
- **CSS Filters**: `grayscale(1)` applied to hero background image, `backdrop-filter: blur(8px)` for frosted glass effects
- **Object-fit**: `object-fit: cover` for images to fill containers
- **Absolute Positioning**: Used for sector card numbers in top-right corner and section divider lines
- **Auto-rotation with timers**: JavaScript `setInterval` and `setTimeout` for automatic tab cycling with proper cleanup

## 4. Relevant Files and Code

### index.html (457 lines)
**Purpose**: Main HTML structure for Altius Lifts website

**Key sections**:
- Topbar with social links and contact info
- Fixed navbar with logo, nav links, and CTA buttons
- Hero section with full-width background image, overlay, and left-aligned content
- Services section with auto-rotating tabs and animated panels
- Sectors section with main feature card and 6 sidebar cards
- FAQ section with Alpine.js accordion
- CTA Partner section with image and text
- Footer with 4-column layout

**Services Section Auto-rotation** (lines 96-142):
