// Navbar scroll effect
const navbar = document.getElementById('navbar');
const topbar = document.getElementById('topbar');
window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
  if (window.scrollY > 50) {
    navbar.classList.add('scrolled');
    if (topbar) topbar.style.transform = 'translateY(-100%)';
  } else {
    navbar.classList.remove('scrolled');
    if (topbar) topbar.style.transform = 'translateY(0)';
  }
});
if (topbar) topbar.style.transition = 'transform 0.3s ease';
```

## 5. Problem Solving

**Issues Resolved**:
1. Auto-rotation timer stacking - Fixed by adding proper cleanup with `delay` timer tracking and `restart()` method
2. List animation timing too slow - Reduced gap from 1s to 0.45s and adjusted stagger from 0.08s to 0.1s
3. Service tab gradients too dark - Created new `--dark-mid` variable
4. Code bloat - Removed 272 lines (16%) through systematic audit and cleanup
5. Navigation became mobile at 768px but should be 1024px - Fixed by moving breakpoint
6. Hero CTAs stacked at 768px unnecessarily - Removed stacking rule
7. Horizontal overflow at certain widths - Fixed by adding `flex-wrap: nowrap` at 768px for service tabs and `overflow-x: hidden` on `html`
8. Sectors section layout didn't follow specified responsive behavior - Fixed with proper breakpoint cascade
9. Footer grid didn't follow specified 3-tier responsive layout - Fixed with proper grid changes at each breakpoint
10. Content-grid padding was 1.5rem but needed to be 3rem - Changed `--padding-inline` to 3rem (reduced to 1.5rem at ≤480px)
11. Hero buttons should stack below 460px - Added breakpoint with column direction and full-width stretch
12. Service tabs became 1 column at 768px but should wait until 600px - Moved stacking rules to 600px breakpoint
13. Hero content had misaligned left edge vs. rest of page - Moved `--padding-inline` to `:root`, removed duplicate padding from `.hero-content`, changed `#hero` to use `var(--padding-inline)`
14. Hero buttons needed to be full width when stacked - Added `align-items: stretch` and centered text
15. Hero CTAs had bottom margin that should be controlled by section padding - Removed `margin-bottom: 60px`
16. Hero section needed different padding on large screens and at 768px - Set desktop to 180px top / 120px bottom, 768px to 140px top
17. Topbar and navbar had alignment issues with content-grid - Changed both to use `var(--padding-inline)` and `calc(var(--container) + var(--padding-inline) * 2)` for max-width, achieving 0px difference at all widths
18. **Content-grid not single source of truth** - Refactored `#topbar`, `#navbar`, and `#hero` to use content-grid with breakout children, removed all custom width systems (`max-width`, `margin: 0 auto`, `padding`), removed `--container` variable
19. **Sector-main stretching to sidebar height at 960px** - Added `height: 60%; align-self: start` at ≤960px, reset to `height: 380px; align-self: auto` at ≤768px
20. **Sector-main and sector-sidebar order at 768px** - Used CSS `order` property to swap positions (sidebar first, main second)
21. **FAQ header center-aligned** - Removed `text-align: center` from `.faq-header` and `margin: 0 auto` from `.faq-list`
22. **FAQ section needed image** - Created 2-column layout with `.faq-layout` grid, added `.faq-img` with `/lift-accessability.jpg`, stacks to single column at ≤768px

## 6. Pending Tasks and Next Steps

**Current Status**: The FAQ section image has been successfully added. The page now has a 2-column FAQ layout on desktop with the accordion on the left and the accessibility image on the right. At mobile widths (≤768px), it stacks to single column with the image below the accordion.

