5. **Creating src/main.js entry point** - COMPLETED
   - Imports all CSS files in order: base.css → components.css → home.css
   - Contains navbar scroll effect JavaScript

6. **Updating index.html** - IN PROGRESS (NEXT TASK)
   - Need to add `<script type="module" src="/src/main.js"></script>` before `</body>`
   - Need to remove old `<link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css" />`
   - Need to remove old `<script src="/main.js"></script>`
   - Need to add utility classes to HTML elements:
     - Add `.section-heading` to h2 elements in: `.sc-header`, `.sectors-header`, `.faq-header`, `.cta-partner-text`
     - Add `.img-cover` to img elements in: `.placeholder-img`, `.sc-panel-img`, `.faq-img`
     - Add `.section-dark` to sections: `#services`, `#sectors`, `#cta-partner`
     - Add `.arrow-link` to `.sc-cta` and `.view-more` elements

7. **Clean up & verify** - PENDING
   - Remove old `style.css` from root
   - Remove old `main.js` from root
   - Test dev server: `npm run dev`
   - Verify build: `npm run build`
   - Check for visual parity
   - Verify all images load correctly from `public/`
   - Check console for errors
   - Test responsive breakpoints
   - Verify Alpine.js functionality

**Direct quote from most recent work:**
The AI created a task list with 8 tasks and confirmed: "Yes — sorry, I was reading through the full codebase planning the restructure. Let me get moving."

The AI has completed tasks 1-5 and is currently on task 6: "Update index.html - Add Vite module script, add utility classes (.section-heading, .img-cover, .section-dark, .arrow-link) to HTML elements, remove old link/script tags"

## 3. Key Technical Concepts

- **Vite**: Modern build tool used for development server with hot module replacement - configured with `npm run dev`, `npm run build`, `npm run preview` scripts
- **Vite Module Entry Point**: Uses `src/main.js` as entry point to import all CSS files and JS modules
- **Vanilla JavaScript**: Used for navbar scroll effects
- **Alpine.js 3.x**: Lightweight JavaScript framework for reactive interactivity
- **Alpine.js x-intersect plugin**: Intersection Observer wrapper for scroll-triggered animations
- **Alpine.js x-collapse plugin**: Smooth height animation for accordions
- **Alpine.js x-data, x-show, x-transition, x-init, x-effect, :class**: Directives for state management, transitions, and reactive classes
- **CSS Custom Properties**: Used for theming (colors, spacing, radii) and animation timing
- **OKLCH Color Space**: CSS Color Level 4 color space - provides perceptually uniform colors with better interpolation than RGB/HSL
- **Relative Color Syntax**: `oklch(from var(--overlay) l c h / 0.75)` - used for hero overlay gradient
- **CSS Grid**: Primary layout system for sections
- **Content-Grid Layout System**: Kevin Powell / Ryan Mulligan intrinsic layout pattern using CSS Grid with named grid lines for content/breakout/full-width control. This is the **single source of truth** for horizontal widths and alignment across the entire site.
- **Flexbox**: Used for navbar, hero stats, and smaller component layouts
- **CSS Animations**: `@keyframes` for hero on-load animations and service panel content animations, CSS transitions for scroll-triggered animations
- **Intersection Observer API**: Wrapped by Alpine.js x-intersect plugin
- **Fixed Positioning**: Used for topbar and navbar with scroll behavior
- **CSS Gradients**: Linear gradients used for section backgrounds, navbar, footer, and service tabs
- **Font Awesome 6.5.1**: Icon library loaded via CDN
- **Cubic Bezier Easing**: `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)` stored in `--ease-out-expo` variable
