12. **FOUC (Flash of Unstyled Content)** - Module script was at bottom of body, moved to head to block rendering until CSS loads

**Current Challenge - SOLVED**:
The user reported a flash of unstyled content when the page loads. This was caused by the `<script type="module" src="/src/main.js">` being placed at the bottom of `<body>`. The browser would render the full HTML before the module loaded and injected the CSS.

