Here's the full mechanism now:

**`src/main.js`** — primary trigger (fires once the module loads, CSS is already injected):
````javascript path=src/main.js mode=EXCERPT
// ===== FOUC Prevention =====
document.body.classList.add('loaded');
````

**`index.html` `<head>`** — critical inline CSS (hides body immediately):
````html path=index.html mode=EXCERPT
  <style>
    body { visibility: hidden; }
    body.loaded { visibility: visible; }
  </style>
````

**`index.html` bottom of `<body>`** — fallback (safety net if module fails):
````html path=index.html mode=EXCERPT
<script>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
    setTimeout(function() { document.body.classList.add('loaded'); }, 50);
  });
  setTimeout(function() { document.body.classList.add('loaded'); }, 500);
</script>
````

The flow is:
1. Browser parses `<head>` → inline `<style>` hides body instantly
2. Vite module loads → CSS gets injected → `document.body.classList.add('loaded')` reveals the page (styled)
3. If the module somehow fails, the inline fallback at the bottom adds `.loaded` after 50ms (DOMContentLoaded) or 500ms (absolute timeout)

Give it a hard refresh and the FOUC should be gone.

